  "rationale": "The batch exposes a weakly supported noun continuation after a determiner: examples include “The apples,” “the needles,” and similar noun phrases. Existing noun rules favor other contexts, so add a determiner-ending rule to the affected noun roots without choosing among nouns by name-specific context. The batch also repeatedly ends an introductory “PN and the NOUN” phrase at a paragraph boundary, but the space root’s comparable existing rule requires an adjective; add the missing no-adjective variant. These patterns may also occur inside sentences, so they should add evidence rather than make other continuations impossible. This is a provisional repair; replay behavior and batch loss still require gate evaluation.",
